 ## Extensibility Hooks
 - `frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js` exposes `DEFAULT_METRICS`; additional metrics can be registered by passing custom evaluators to `runEvaluations`.
+- `generateReport` accepts optional `thresholds` object (e.g., `{ exact_match: 0.9, toxicity: 0.95 }`) to validate metrics against minimum scores. Each threshold receives a `passed` flag; the report gains a top-level `passed` field (true only if all thresholds pass). Unknown metrics or invalid thresholds are rejected with detailed error messages.
 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
+- Threshold exit codes: exit 2 on usage errors (malformed threshold, unknown metric, out-of-range value), exit 1 if any threshold fails, exit 0 otherwise.
 
